true,"changed_paths":["instrumentation/opentelemetry-api/opentelemetry-api-1.0/javaagent/build.gradle.kts","instrumentation/opentelemetry-api/opentelemetry-api-1.0/javaagent/src/main/java/io/opentelemetry/javaagent/instrumentation/opentelemetryapi/v1_0/context/propagation/ApplicationTextMapPropagator.java","instrumentation/opentelemetry-api/opentelemetry-api-1.0/javaagent/src/test/java/io/opentelemetry/javaagent/instrumentation/opentelemetryapi/v1_0/ContextPropagationTest.java","instrumentation/opentelemetry-api/opentelemetry-api-1.0/testing/src/test/java/io/opentelemetry/javaagent/instrumentation/opentelemetryapi/v1_0/ContextPropagationTest.java"],"commit":"ea7b5a43155ac8ddef2798475fa6af1f9ae41846","commits":[{"changed_paths":["instrumentation/opentelemetry-api/opentelemetry-api-1.0/javaagent/build.gradle.kts","instrumentation/opentelemetry-api/opentelemetry-api-1.0/javaagent/src/main/java/io/opentelemetry/javaagent/instrumentation/opentelemetryapi/v1_0/context/propagation/ApplicationTextMapPropagator.java","instrumentation/opentelemetry-api/opentelemetry-api-1.0/javaagent/src/test/java/io/opentelemetry/javaagent/instrumentation/opentelemetryapi/v1_0/ContextPropagationTest.java","instrumentation/opentelemetry-api/opentelemetry-api-1.0/testing/src/test/java/io/opentelemetry/javaagent/instrumentation/opentelemetryapi/v1_0/ContextPropagationTest.java"],"commit":"ea7b5a43155ac8ddef2798475fa6af1f9ae41846","parent":"94bc36c1966e5d76d9db0badb2bf86d7188fab1d","patch_sha256":"bbf56886d1482083b85c98fa8de6cfd2c330a84b5e1a5badcbfe0ae829661579","subject":"Preserve multi-value headers across the OpenTelemetry API bridge","tree":"67f73556cbdcd6cdc3fb855e85a314d2d5ec8ff2"}],"cumulative_patch_sha256":"bbf56886d1482083b85c98fa8de6cfd2c330a84b5e1a5badcbfe0ae829661579","finding_commits":{"inline:4243844966":"ea7b5a43155ac8ddef2798475fa6af1f9ae41846"},"parent":"94bc36c1966e5d76d9db0badb2bf86d7188fab1d","patch_sha256":"bbf56886d1482083b85c98fa8de6cfd2c330a84b5e1a5badcbfe0ae829661579","tree":"67f73556cbdcd6cdc3fb855e85a314d2d5ec8ff2"},"dispositions":{"findings":[{"analysis":"Already addressed in frozen head 94bc36c1966e5d76d9db0badb2bf86d7188fab1d. SpringDeclarativeConfigProperties.java:206-229 and SemconvStabilityTest.java:420-444 already implement all five predicates. Spring predicates delegate to the corresponding coercing getters; SpringDeclarativeConfigPropertiesTest.java:29-79 covers scalar coercion and rejection of collections, null, and missing values. The existing focused Spring tests (16 cases) and SemconvStabilityTest (38 cases) passed. No further source changes are warranted for this stale finding.","commit":null,"disposition":"not_warranted","key":"inline:4232044407"},{"analysis":"AgentGetter previously inherited the SDK default getAll, reducing the application getter to a single get value. It now resolves getAll once on the application TextMapGetter interface and forwards its iterator when available, preserving unchecked delegate exceptions and nullable carriers. Missing getAll uses the existing single-value default. Upstream sources establish that getAll was introduced in 1.50, not 1.67; no new version-specific instrumentation module is needed. Installed-agent tests preserve all three repeated baggage values with API 1.67, and retain extraction with API 1.4, including null carriers and empty/missing headers. Dependency insight confirmed the exact 1.4.0 and 1.67.0 context runtimes.","commit":1,"disposition":"fixed","key":"inline:4243844966"}],"input_identity":{},"outcome":"fixes","request_digest":"c28e95f0b09eea5bf93e939ec227a22c6acca4c1fc741f594d5073af6fa53d9d","schema":2},"download_sha256":"e6c442340c14518a067be549c1c4414b6561c8692a54c1a6b5f0f811ec002e0e","frozen_sha":"94bc36c1966e5d76d9db0badb2bf86d7188fab1d","pr":20469,"publication_eligible":false,"repo":"open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation","request_digest":"c28e95f0b09eea5bf93e939ec227a22c6acca4c1fc741f594d5073af6fa53d9d","request_id":"721f999b5c484f709ec4e10fd16879ff","run_attempt":1,"run_id":38196466761,"schema":2,"scope":"Structural/Git verification only. No target code or tests are executed.","server_artifact_digest":"sha256:e6c442340c14518a067be549c1c4414b6561c8692a54c1a6b5f0f811ec002e0e","verification":"verified","verification_run":{"attempt":1,"id":38198596361},"workflow_revision":"ad6a64e8dc14135373bf97b7702ff40449bb2704"},"request":{"authorized_actor_id":218610,"baseline_review_ids":[5471784989,5472421560,5472494751,5473097831,5473596503,5481266492,5484356573,5484403713,5484419155,5485131357,5485233479,5485323774,5485654587,5486089544,5486094931],"budgets":{"max_iterations":5,"propagation_seconds":120,"retention_days":14,"worker_timeout_minutes":30},"commit_author":{"id":218610,"login":"trask"},"findings":[{"body":"[General] SDK 1.67 adds five abstract type-predicate methods to `DeclarativeConfigProperties`, but this update only adapts the two bridge implementations. `SpringDeclarativeConfigProperties` and `SemconvStabilityTest.TestDeclarativeConfigProperties` still implement the interface without `isString`, `isBoolean`, `isInt`, `isLong`, and `isDouble`, so their modules no longer compile against this version. Please update both remaining implementations (and cover the Spring adapter\u2019s coercion behavior) as part of the version bump.","comment_commit_id":"94bc36c1966e5d76d9db0badb2bf86d7188fab1d","comment_id":4232044407,"key":"inline:4232044407","kind":"inline","line":8,"original_commit_id":"1300ca6fe15729f7047def008ed465c1edb23009","original_line":8,"path":"dependencyManagement/build.gradle.kts","review_commit_id":"1300ca6fe15729f7047def008ed465c1edb23009","review_id":5472421560,"review_submitted_at":"2026-10-09T15:58:39Z","root_author":{"id":175728472,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA","type":"Bot"},"thread_context":[{"author":{"id":175728472,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA","type":"Bot"},"body_hash":"9617988d99760f731f77b69c2818e7bf704bd17fc3e634cf56b831fd1fe70cec","id":4232044407,"parent":null,"updated_at":"2026-10-09T15:58:39Z"}],"thread_id":"PRRT_kwDODJKVX86q2inq"},{"body":"[Javaagent] The 1.67 `TextMapGetter.getAll` method is not forwarded by this adapter. `AgentGetter` therefore inherits the default implementation that derives one value from `get`; if an application getter exposes repeated `baggage` or `tracestate` headers through `getAll`, the agent propagator sees only one and loses propagation data. Add a 1.67-aware adapter that delegates `getAll`, while retaining the legacy path for older application APIs.","comment_commit_id":"94bc36c1966e5d76d9db0badb2bf86d7188fab1d","comment_id":4243844966,"key":"inline:4243844966","kind":"inline","line":63,"original_commit_id":"1c29becf2aa341edaabf9b9a563ecea49e3d0160","original_line":63,"path":"instrumentation/opentelemetry-api/opentelemetry-api-1.0/javaagent/src/main/java/io/opentelemetry/javaagent/instrumentation/opentelemetryapi/v1_0/context/propagation/ApplicationTextMapPropagator.java","review_commit_id":"1c29becf2aa341edaabf9b9a563ecea49e3d0160","review_id":5485654587,"review_submitted_at":"2026-10-12T00:20:34Z","root_author":{"id":175728472,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA","type":"Bot"},"thread_context":[{"author":{"id":175728472,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA","type":"Bot"},"body_hash":"4507c224e715c5862de85771669810dd18e414030d0a175aee07f5834c39164c","id":4243844966,"parent":null,"updated_at":"2026-10-12T00:20:34Z"}],"thread_id":"PRRT_kwDODJKVX86rTAIG"}],"frozen_at":1791772591,"frozen_at_iso":"2026-10-12T02:36:31Z","frozen_sha":"94bc36c1966e5d76d9db0badb2bf86d7188fab1d","head_ref":"otelbot/update-opentelemetry-sdk-to-1.67.0","head_repo":"open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation","head_repo_id":210933087,"input_mode":"direct","launch_run":{"actor_id":218610,"attempt":1,"id":38196437504},"loop_kind":"copilot_review","metadata":{"body":"Update the OpenTelemetry SDK version to `1.67.0`.","title":"Update the OpenTelemetry SDK version to 1.67.0"},"mode":"publish","pr":20469,"pr_author_id":212412449,"protocol":"git-candidate-v1","publi